invariant: INV-16
file: build.zig
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: build.zig takes WIDEMUL=runtime beside X25519=wide, which the
  Makefile refuses, so the two builds stop refusing the same values. ct.h
  still stops the compile, but the Zig build writes both defines first,
  and test/zig-build-check.sh compares only values both builds accept, so
  only the refusal check objects.

--- old
    if (config.widemul == .runtime and config.x25519 == .wide) {
        fatal("WIDEMUL=runtime asks each session for the multiply's timing, and X25519=wide states it at build time; use X25519=portable", .{});
    }
--- new
